  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the function $f(x)=\\cos x^{2}$. Then,",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7vIFO",
      "text": "$f$ is of period $2 \\pi$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fMV4V",
      "text": "$f$ is of period $\\sqrt{2 \\pi}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rUAKv",
      "text": "$f$ is not periodic",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6ODud",
      "text": "$f$ is of period $\\pi$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,\r\n$$\r\nf(x)=\\cos x^{2}\r\n$$\r\nLet $T$ be the period of $f(x)$. Then\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n& & f(x+T) &=f(x) \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow & & \\cos (x+T)^{2} &=\\cos x^{2}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\nBut there is no value of $T$ for which\r\n$$\r\n\\cos (x+T)^{2}=\\cos x^{2}\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore f(x)$ is not periodic",
    "image": null
  },
